---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Kitchener Peckford: commission plans, the data models behind them, and a lot of curiosity.">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About me</h1>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I help companies determine why and how to pay their employees commissions. Above that, I
        build the actual data model that services it, and all of the other pieces behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Let’s say for every candy bar you sold to people, I was to pay you 20 cents. That would be
        easy. Now let’s make it more complex: I let you dictate the cost of every candy bar, but I
        will only pay you a commission on a percentage above 3 dollars. This alone is complex to
        figure out. Now imagine there are several more layers to this problem, and then doing it
        for 40,000 employees.
      </p>
      <p>I build the data model to do these calculations consistently.</p>

      <h2>Something I believe</h2>
      <p>
        As consultants, especially at the technical level, we are told our job is to do the
        technical piece. But the more I get into this type of job, the more I see it’s not just
        about the technical aspect. It’s about being able to articulate it, so that once you’re
        done working on your piece, you can pass it off to someone and they can understand it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m not the best at that. I know a lot of people feel like it’s a waste of time, but I
        think it’s so important. If it was any other product, like a consumer product, it would get
        so much pushback. But because it’s consulting, we kind of just forget it. And I think
        that’s just so ridiculous.
      </p>

      <h2>Things I could talk about for hours</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How AI is changing the landscape of everything we do.</li>
        <li>Bikes, and the biking scene I grew up in.</li>
        <li>
          Working with small businesses to figure out how to grow their businesses. Anytime I get
          to talk to a friend about how to automate pieces of their business or how to look at
          analytics, I love those conversations, and I’m working on those types of things.
        </li>
        <li>Sports. I play ball hockey twice a week, and I love just keeping active.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Things that surprise people</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>I’m not actually named after the city.</li>
        <li>
          I don’t have the typical background you’d expect for where I work. A lot of my friends
          look at the situation and ask, why is Kitchener doing what he’s doing? He was never good
          at math. For me, I was just curious, and that’s how I got into all this.
        </li>
        <li>I’m incredibly curious, and I don’t stop thinking about things.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="contact">Get in touch</h2>
      <ul class="contact">
        {SITE.email && <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>}
        <li>LinkedIn: <a href={SITE.linkedin} rel="me noopener">linkedin.com/in/kpeckford</a></li>
        {SITE.github && <li>GitHub: <a href={SITE.github} rel="me noopener">{SITE.github.replace('https://', '')}</a></li>}
        <li>RSS: <a href="/rss.xml">subscribe to new posts</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.contact { list-style: none; padding: 0; } .contact li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }</style>
